    "final_answer": "Based on my investigation, I now have the answer. Looking at the Hugging Face datasets page filtered by Audio modality and sorted by \"Most downloads\", the top result is clear.\n\n**Recording the key findings:**\n- Page filtered by: Audio modality (`modality=modality%3Aaudio`)\n- Sorted by: Most downloads\n- Top dataset: **ACERobotics/ACE-Data-0** with 256k downloads (Updated Sept 11, 2026)\n- The dataset has Video, Audio, and 3D modalities (confirmed by clicking into the dataset)\n- It is tagged with \"audio\" task\n\n## Answer\n\nThe most downloaded audio-related dataset on Hugging Face currently is:\n\n**ACERobotics/ACE-Data-0** with approximately **256,000 downloads**\n\nThis dataset is a multimodal robotics/embodied AI dataset that includes audio as one of its modalities (alongside Video and 3D), and it appears at the top of the audio-modality-filtered, sorted-by-downloads list on the Hugging Face Datasets page.\n\nFor comparison, here are the next most-downloaded audio-related datasets:\n| Rank | Dataset | Downloads |\n|------|---------|-----------|\n| 1 | ACERobotics/ACE-Data-0 | 256k |\n| 2 | fixie-ai/common_voice_17_0 | 216k |\n| 3 | facebook/seamless-interaction | 135k |\n| 4 | ylacombe/cml-tts | 123k |\n| 5 | google/fleurs | 101k |\n\nNote: If interpreting \"audio-related\" strictly as a primarily-audio (speech/music) dataset, then `fixie-ai/common_voice_17_0` (a Mozilla Common Voice speech dataset) would be the answer with 216k downloads.",
